course: dictionary
lesson: 10353
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word transplant can be a noun (a thing, like an operation) or a verb (an action, like moving something). In «The doctors planned a heart transplant», transplant is a noun, an operation. The words before it, heart and doctors, are your clues.
explain: Look at the sentence around the word. A gardener might say, «We transplant seedlings into the garden.» There are no doctors or hearts, so transplant must mean to dig up a small plant and plant it somewhere else. Always ask: does this sentence talk about medicine, gardening, or moving house?
explain: The wood frog sentence gives its own clue. «The wood frog lets about two thirds of the water in its body freeze; its heart stops, and sugar works as antifreeze inside its cells until it thaws in spring; doctors study it to learn how to keep organs for transplant, body parts given to sick people, cold for longer.» The words after the comma explain transplant: body parts given to sick people. You do not need to stop and look it up.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A transplant can be an operation in which a damaged organ, such as a heart or kidney, is replaced with a healthy one from a donor.
fact: To transplant can also mean to dig up a plant and plant it somewhere else, such as moving seedlings from pots into the garden.
fact: An organ donor is a person who gives an organ, either after death or, for a kidney, while still alive, so that a sick person can get a transplant.
fact: To transplant can also mean to move people or things to a new place to live.
exercise: «The doctors planned a kidney transplant for the sick man.» What is a transplant in this sentence? | A type of frog that lives in woods | *An operation that replaces a damaged kidney with a healthy one | A bag for carrying tools | A school trip to the hospital
exercise: Gardeners transplant seedlings from small pots into the garden. What does transplant mean here? | Cut the plants down to the ground | Paint the pots in bright colours | Water the plants until they grow tall | *Dig up a plant and plant it somewhere else
exercise: «...doctors study it to learn how to keep organs for transplant, body parts given to sick people, cold for longer.» What does transplant mean in this sentence? | A long journey by boat | *Body parts given to sick people | A kind of ice | The garden where the frogs live
test: What is an organ donor? | A doctor who only works in gardens | Someone who gives an organ to help a sick person | *Someone who gives an organ to help a sick person, either after death or a kidney while alive | A person who lives in a big house
test: In «The family decided to transplant to a new town next year», what does transplant mean? | *To move to a new place to live | To give a kidney to a friend | To cut the grass | To dig up a tree in the park
exam: In «Ella said the transplant went well and her heart is strong now», what is a transplant? | A walk through the garden | A type of seed planted in spring | *An operation that replaces a damaged heart with a healthy one | A gift of sweets to the nurse
